   "text": "The first three files, in order, are:\n\n1. `exllamav3/__init__.py`\n2. `exllamav3/architecture/__init__.py`\n3. `exllamav3/architecture/afmoe.py`\n\nThe first file, `exllamav3/__init__.py`, is the package entry point for exllamav3. It sets environment defaults before importing torch (disabling the ROCm profiler registration thread by default), raises a clear error if PyTorch is missing, and configures the CUDA caching allocator to use expandable segments unless the user has already set allocator options or is on Windows/ROCm. It also points Triton at the AMD backend on ROCm builds, then re-exports the library's main public API (Config, Model, Tokenizer, Cache, Generator, samplers, etc.) so users can import them directly from `exllamav3`."
  },
  "8192": {
   "prompt_tokens": 8192,
   "prompt_sha256": "98294f87c7dfaef25eac4def710a98da04dc0edda2dca1a6c463e0a9684cba7d",
   "ttft_s": 10.69,
   "prefill_tok_s": 766.6,
   "completion_tokens": 236,
   "decode_s": 11.05,
   "decode_tok_s": 21.26,
   "finish": "stop",
   "text_sha256": "5bb1876b85184798eadbe845ee7bf546911fa1962c3f6963e9c8b4627a809f5e",
   "text": "The first three files, in order, are:\n\n1. `exllamav3/__init__.py`\n2. `exllamav3/architecture/__init__.py`\n3. `exllamav3/architecture/afmoe.py`\n\nThe very first file, `exllamav3/__init__.py`, is the package's top-level entry point. It sets environment defaults before importing torch (disabling the ROCm profiler registration thread and pointing Triton at the AMD backend on ROCm builds), imports torch with a helpful error message if it's missing, and configures the CUDA caching allocator to use expandable segments unless the user has already set `PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF` or is on Windows/ROCm. It then re-exports the library's public API \u2014 `Config`, `Model`, `Tokenizer`, `MMEmbedding`, the cache classes, `Generator`/`Job`/`AsyncGenerator`/`AsyncJob` and the filter classes, plus the sampler module \u2014 so users can access everything from the `exllamav3` namespace."
  },
  "32768": {
   "prompt_tokens": 32768,
   "prompt_sha256": "fcc5374c6f0b1a39129148f5fab3c035f332097f59083060b14349bbbd76c4fa",
   "ttft_s": 39.95,
   "prefill_tok_s": 820.2,
   "completion_tokens": 256,
   "decode_s": 12.58,
   "decode_tok_s": 20.27,
   "finish": "stop",
   "text_sha256": "4cfed955127b0c7039e63054bda4c9526bd026c038d445f378678e24036cd3ae",
   "text": "The first three files, in order, are:\n\n1. `exllamav3/__init__.py`\n2. `exllamav3/architecture/__init__.py`\n3. `exllamav3/architecture/afmoe.py`\n\nThe first file is the package's top-level entry point. It sets two environment defaults before importing torch \u2014 disabling the ROCm profiler registration (which otherwise leaves an HSA event thread spinning) and, on ROCm builds, pointing Triton at its AMD backend \u2014 then configures the CUDA caching allocator to use expandable segments (skipped on Windows, ROCm, or when the user has already set `PYTORCH_CUDA_ALLOC_CONF`). It raises a clear error if torch is missing, explaining that exllamav3 deliberately doesn't install a default torch because it must match the user's CUDA setup. Finally, it re-exports the library's public API: `Config`, `Model`, `Tokenizer`, `MMEmbedding`, the cache layer classes, and the generator classes (`Generator`, `Job`, `AsyncGenerator`, `AsyncJob`, `Filter`, `FormatronFilter`, `LLGuidanceFilter`) plus the sampler module."
  }
